                <pb facs="1121" n="1061" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg1061"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Sullivan.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 38.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-03-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 31, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch of January 20, 1868, No. 49, inclosing copies of your correspondence
                    with the government of the United States of Colombia on the subject of the
                    Panama commercial war tax.</p>
                <p>The instructions of this department, under date of June 13, 1867, were made
                    necessary mainly by the doubt which then existed whether the threatened
                    resistance by the State of Panama to troops acting under the orders of General
                    Mosquera was to be regarded as rebellion against the legitimate government of
                    the United States of Colombia. The progress of events having resolved that doubt
                    in favor of the State of Panama, the further discussion of the general question
                    of the liabilty of our citizens to extraordinary taxes may be postponed to some
                    future occasion.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peter</hi> J. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Sullivan,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
